# secret-scan.allow — documented false positives for scripts/gates/secret-scan.sh
#
# One entry per line, tab-separated, four fields:
#   rule<TAB>path-ERE<TAB>value-ERE-or-<TAB>reason
#
#   rule       the rule id (token-prefix, high-entropy, pem, private-url,
#              private-host, home-path, game-data, big-binary)
#   path-ERE   unanchored ERE matched against the tracked file path. For
#              --history findings it may instead be commit=<sha-prefix>:
#              <path-glob>, which matches only that commit (sha prefix), so
#              an already-pushed, since-fixed leak can be blessed for that
#              commit alone — the gate still fails on any NEW occurrence
#              (a new commit is a new sha and matches no commit= entry)
#   value      ERE the extracted matched value must also match, or * for any
#              value (or any detail) from that path under that rule
#   reason     why this is a documented false positive (AGENTS.md rule 5:
#              synthetic fixtures and documented examples only — never a
#              real credential, real private endpoint, or real home path)
#
# Every entry below corresponds to a synthetic test fixture or a documented
# device/example path. If a value here ever stops being synthetic, remove the
# entry and fix the content — the gate must not bless real secrets.

token-prefix	internal/auth/service_test\.go	*	synthetic bad token in the auth rejection test (must be rejected; never real)
token-prefix	internal/support/redact_test\.go	*	redactor's own test fixtures: synthetic tokens the redaction code must detect
high-entropy	internal/support/redact_test\.go	*	redactor's own test fixtures: synthetic token value the redaction code must detect
private-url	internal/support/redact_test\.go	*	redactor's own test fixtures: synthetic private endpoints the redaction code must detect
private-url	internal/web/web_test\.go	*	URL-validation test fixtures: synthetic RFC 1918 / .local / .internal hosts proving the SSRF blocklist
private-url	internal/auth/policy_test\.go	*	synthetic .local hostnames for the gateway URL policy tests
private-url	internal/support/sections_test\.go	*	synthetic gateway URL test fixture (t.Setenv)
private-url	internal/web/search/searxng\.go	*	doc-comment example of the SearXNG base URL shape (synthetic host)
home-path	internal/support/redact_test\.go	*	redactor's own test fixtures: synthetic home paths the redaction code must detect (username appears only inside a synthetic log line)
home-path	docs/release\.md	/home/arduino/	documented UNO Q device data layout (device username, not personal data)
home-path	docs/manuals/19-install-on-uno-q\.md	/home/arduino/	documented UNO Q device data layout (device username, not personal data)
home-path	internal/bootstrap/bootstrap_test\.go	*	synthetic /home/tester fixture for the data-dir default tests
home-path	internal/doctor/render_test\.go	*	synthetic /home/user fixture in the rendered-report test
home-path	scripts/release/lifecycle-on-device\.sh	/home/arduino/	documented UNO Q device data backup path in the release lifecycle docs
home-path	scripts/release/lifecycle-remote\.sh	/home/arduino/	documented UNO Q device data path the lifecycle script manages (device username)
home-path	scripts/release/scan-artifacts\.sh	/home/someuser/	self-test planted fixture the artifact scanner must catch (synthetic)
pem	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^-----BEGIN[ ]RSA[ ]PRIVATE[ ]KEY-----$	self-test planted fixture of the pem rule (the value field is written with [ ] classes so this allow file does not self-trip)
private-url	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^https://[g]ateway[.]lan:$	self-test planted fixture of the private-url rule (synthetic, never a real endpoint; bracket forms stop this allow file self-tripping)
private-url	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^https://node123[.]ts[.]net/$	self-test planted fixture of the private-url rule (synthetic, never a real endpoint; bracket forms stop this allow file self-tripping)
home-path	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^/home/planteduser/$	self-test planted fixture of the home-path rule (synthetic)
home-path	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.allow	^/home/(arduino|someuser|planteduser)/$	the allow file's own value fields, which must name the documented/synthetic home paths they bless; written here as one anchored alternation (device username and synthetic fixtures, never personal data)
token-prefix	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	*	the scanner's own rule definitions (metacharacter patterns; no sample secrets in this file)
private-url	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^https://192\.168\.42\.7$	self-test planted fixture of the private-url rule (synthetic, never a real endpoint)
private-host	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^10\.1\.2\.3$	self-test planted fixture: the scanner must detect this in the self-test repo (synthetic, never a real host)
private-host	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^192\.168\.4\.5$	self-test planted fixture: the scanner must detect this in the self-test repo (synthetic, never a real host)
private-host	scripts/gates/secret-scan\.sh	^192\.168\.42\.7$	self-test planted fixture of the private-url rule (synthetic, never a real host)
private-host	internal/api/auth_test\.go	*	synthetic test host in the auth flow tests (fixture, never a real endpoint)
private-host	internal/auth/policy_test\.go	*	synthetic hosts in the gateway URL policy test table (fixtures)
private-host	internal/auth/service_test\.go	*	synthetic host for the setup-not-local rejection test (fixture)
private-host	internal/support/redact_test\.go	*	redactor's own test fixtures: synthetic private hosts the redaction code must detect
private-host	internal/web/policy\.go	*	doc-comment example of the cidr allow-entry shape (synthetic range, not an endpoint)
private-host	internal/web/web_test\.go	*	URL-validation test fixtures: synthetic RFC 1918 hosts proving the SSRF blocklist
private-host	commit=398cad0624b0:.*	^10\.0\.0\.139$	PUBLIC HISTORY, FIXED: commit 398cad0 shipped the UNO Q appliance's LAN address as a bare user@ip ssh target in an ADR, a manual, and a usage string; replaced by a placeholder in 2ef5bc5 (2026-10-18); history cannot be rewritten (pushed, public), so this commit-scoped entry documents the one-time leak while the gate still fails on any new occurrence (a new commit never matches commit=398cad0624b0). The address itself is deliberately not repeated in this file: the gate must not print it.
private-url	internal/providers/redirect_test\.go	*	redirect-policy test fixtures: synthetic RFC 1918 / .internal hosts proving provider clients refuse off-host redirects (ADR 0068)
private-host	internal/providers/redirect_test\.go	*	redirect-policy test fixtures: synthetic RFC 1918 hosts proving provider clients refuse off-host redirects (ADR 0068)
game-data	testdata/disc/synth-windwaker\.gcm	*	synthetic disc built by windwaker.SynthDiscImage with 4 invented lines ("… disc line N"); only the game id and archive names are real identifiers; pinned by TestSyntheticDiscFixture (ADR 0066)
home-path	skills/uno-q-setup/references/[a-z-]+\.md	/home/arduino/	documented UNO Q device data layout in the setup skill (stock board username, not personal data; same as manual 19)
private-host	internal/api/(dev_actions|diagnostics)_test\.go	*	redaction tests: synthetic fake secrets, private hosts and home paths that the redactor must strip (asserted absent from the output)
private-url	internal/api/(dev_actions|diagnostics)_test\.go	*	redaction tests: synthetic fake secrets, private hosts and home paths that the redactor must strip (asserted absent from the output)
token-prefix	internal/api/(dev_actions|diagnostics)_test\.go	*	redaction tests: synthetic fake secrets, private hosts and home paths that the redactor must strip (asserted absent from the output)
home-path	internal/api/(dev_actions|diagnostics)_test\.go	*	redaction tests: synthetic fake secrets, private hosts and home paths that the redactor must strip (asserted absent from the output)
private-host	internal/api/tailnet_test\.go	^192\.168\.1\.40$	synthetic non-tailnet LAN fixture (eth0) in the tailnet-detection unit tests; the tailnet addresses themselves are in Tailscale's documented 100.64.0.0/10 CGNAT range (synthetic, never a real host)
private-url	docs/adr/0109-settings-theme-page-and-tailnet-surface\.md	*	documented example of the tailnet URL shape (UX-13, ADR-0109): the <tailnet> placeholder is not a real MagicDNS name
private-url	internal/api/network_test\.go	*	settings network-section unit tests (UX-13, ADR-0109): obviously-fake *.ts.net pin and derived-URL fixtures (uno-q.stable-name / uno-q.e2e-tailnet), never a real endpoint
private-url	web/playwright\.config\.ts	uno-q[.]stable-tailnet[.]example[.]ts[.]net	settings-theme e2e walk's tailnet pin (UX-13, ADR-0109): an obviously-fake stable *.ts.net name the spec asserts text equality against (synthetic, never a real endpoint)
private-url	web/src/pages/Settings\.test\.tsx	uno-q[.]stubbed-tailnet[.]ts[.]net	Settings unit-test fixture (UX-13, ADR-0109): the stubbed tailnet URL the page renders verbatim (synthetic, never a real endpoint)
